  notes: "BLEND SHOWCASE 2D - how this scene works\r\n\r\nPLAY IT\r\n  Press Play.
    Left/Right or A/D (or the on-screen buttons) move between stations.\r\n  Space
    toggles Blend on/off for the station on screen. Blend OFF draws the very same
    layers with plain\r\n  Normal blending, so you see what the blend mode adds.
    The HUD slider sets the opacity of the blended layer.\r\n\r\nHIERARCHY\r\n  Main
    Camera ........... orthographic, moved by the Showcase Controller.\r\n  Showcase
    Controller ... keyboard, HUD buttons, camera glide. Holds the list of stations.\r\n 
    HUD Canvas ............ screen-space overlay: help, Prev/Blend/Next, opacity
    slider, station counter.\r\n  Stations/Station NN ... one per use case, 24 units
    apart along X.\r\n      Canvas (text and controls) ... world-space UI: title,
    'How it works', mode/formula line, live status,\r\n                                    
    plus station-specific controls on the right.\r\n      Demo (generated) .............
    created when Play starts. All sprites and textures are made in code.\r\n     
    Offstage ...................... (some stations) content 200 units below, seen
    only by a station camera\r\n                                     that renders
    it into a RenderTexture for the compositor.\r\n\r\nTWO WAYS TO BLEND\r\n  Fixed-function:
    a normal material using Blend Mode/FixedBlend. The GPU blends it with what is
    already\r\n    on screen. Only 9 modes work this way (Normal, Darken, Multiply,
    Linear burn, Lighten, Screen, Add,\r\n    Exclusion, Subtract), but it is the
    cheapest option and fine for sprites, particles and UI.\r\n  Compositor: BlendLayerStack
    blends texture layers with Blend Mode/BlendCompositor, like Photoshop layers.\r\n   
    All 27 modes. The result is a RenderTexture shown on a quad.\r\n\r\nWHERE THE
    CODE IS\r\n  Assets/BlendModes/Showcase/Runtime/Station.cs ........
    base class, read it first.\r\n  Assets/BlendModes/Showcase/Runtime/Stations/
    ......... one small script per station.\r\n  Assets/BlendModes/Showcase/Runtime/ProcArt.cs
    ........ code-generated art (pixel canvas, noise).\r\n  Assets/Projects/Blend
    Mode/Showcase/Editor/StationDefs.cs ..... the text on every station.\r\n  Rebuild
    this scene: Tools > Blend Mode > Build Showcase Scene."
